       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe and may be a transcription error.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose (1600 mg)** is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **The daily total (6400 mg)** is twice the usual adult maximum of 3200 mg per day.\n\nAt this dose the patient would be at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily**, which is 1600 mg per day. This is common if 1600 mg was meant as the daily total.\n2. **800 mg three or four times daily**, which is 2400\u20133200 mg per day. This is the top of the usual range.\n3. **Something else.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll put it on the order note, though I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
